## Rows skipped (7)

- hi-a 1 P1 003 sentencing. Not applied. RULEBOOK R3 and ACCEPTED-ROUND forbid turning the softened “some judgments / not a guaranteed or typical outcome” line back into “courts generally impose about 3 / 4 / 6 months”. Digits 3, 4, and 6 stay.
- hi-a 3 P2 003 “अधिकतम क्षतिपूर्ति”. Not applied. R3 already replaced “pursue the maximum compensation” with compensation the facts and evidence support. Restoring अधिकतम is a result claim.
- hi-a 10 P2 copyright gloss 著作權. Not applied. guidance-disclosure-parity.test.ts requires every locale in its list, including hi, to carry the same CJK gloss set as Vietnamese. The Vietnamese services sentence has no 著作權. A Hindi-only gloss fails that test, and this lane cannot edit the other locales. Same skip as r4.
- hi-a 22 P2 and hi-b 26 P2 lakh/crore grouping (15,70,000 and the listed TWD/USD amounts, including the team-bio TWD 1,570,000). Not applied. ACCEPTED-ROUND skips lakh grouping because the checker cannot parse it. TWD 1.57M was not in these rows and stays byte-identical.
- hi-b 9 P2 U+200B in 013 and 015. Not applied. checkBlocks requires the target ZWSP count to equal the Korean source, and the Korean 013/015 files have the same zero-width spaces, including lines whose only character is U+200B. Removing them fails blocks. The same characters in 008 and 009 were left for the same reason.
- hi-b 13 P2 018 heading numbers 7→6 and 8→7. Not applied. The English and Korean sources skip 6 the same way. Renumbering changes digits the checker counts, and ACCEPTED-ROUND forbids changing numbers.

No P3 rows in either review.

## Systemic patterns

- Amounts at or above one lakh, Western grouping: 0 changed (skip above).
- Sentencing written as an uncommon result: 0 changed (R3).
- Withholding link still saying only अनुच्छेद 10: 1 link rewritten to name अनुच्छेद 3 and to say it is not व्यवसाय कर अधिनियम का अनुच्छेद 10.
- जब-clause whose result dropped तो: 7 instances. The three quoted guidance sentences, plus 004 (parent company entering Taiwan), 014 (notice when an indefinite-term contract ends), 017 (capital when a company starts motor freight), and 018 (name check when a foreign company forms a subsidiary). Left “तभी … जब”, “जब तक”, statutory “जब” list items in 009, and the 006 line break “जब मालिश की बात होती है,” — those are not a condition followed by a result in the same sentence.
- “In practice” written as प्रथा: 2 instances (002 “व्यवहार में”; 005 Korea remittance rewritten as “अनुमत नहीं है”). “नवीनतम प्रथा” left; that is current administrative practice, not “in practice, it is useful”.
- Exclude / rule out as निकालें: 2 instances, both in 014. 001’s “भागीदारी न निकालें” was row 17, a different mistranslation, and was rewritten separately.
- U+200B: 0 removed (checker).
- Emerging Stock Board without 興櫃: 1 instance in 018.
- Issuer as निर्गमक: 4 instances in 004.
- Simplified 台 inside the Traditional gloss 台灣法人: 1 instance in 005.
- अभिविन्यास for official guidance links: 3 instances in 003.

R2–R10 were already in this Hindi pack from earlier rounds (consultation lock, feminine forms for Wei Tseng, formal आप, Traditional Chinese glosses other than the 台 row above). This pass did not reopen them except where an r5 row or the जब-तो pattern was the same issue. R1/R11 were not redone. The fullwidth colon in 008 is inside the frontmatter `url:` and stays (R16).

## Reviewer got these wrong (not applied)

- hi-a 1: “courts generally impose about 3 / 4 / 6 months” is the advertising-risk sentence R3 already softened. The current line is the required form.
- hi-a 3: “उपलब्ध अधिकतम क्षतिपूर्ति” puts back the maximum-compensation claim R3 removed.
- hi-a 10: the missing 著作權 gloss is real, but a Hindi-only gloss fails the cross-locale gloss-parity test. Sister locales outside that test (ne, bn, ur, ta, my) already gloss it.
- hi-a 22 and hi-b 26: Indian lakh grouping is what a Delhi editor would write, and the checker does not parse it.
- hi-b 9: the zero-width spaces are in the Korean source. They are not a Hindi-only leak.
- hi-b 13: the missing section 6 is in the English source as well. Renumbering would desync the digits from Korean.

